We can express this using the implication operator `=>`, where the premise is that the map does not contain the key (using `\old(this.containsKey(key))` to refer to the state before the call), and the conclusion is that the result is `null`.

Final assert statement:

<code>assert !\old(this.containsKey(key)) => \result == null;</code>
